WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
Elena holds an active Maryland life producer license.

2
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.280
An insurer offers her a producer agreement.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.180
The state license, the business agreement and the insurer appointment are

4
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.640
related but different. The license establishes permitted insurance authority

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.020
in Maryland. The agreement sets working terms.

6
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.300
The appointment documents the insurer relationship.

7
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.260
The insurer must itself be authorized for the business.

8
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.160
An enthusiastic email from a manager is not a reason to

9
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.480
ignore the required documentation or make promises beyond delegated

10
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.500
authority. Verify the role and the permission before acting.

11
00:00:41.202 --> 00:00:45.622
Maryland permits a licensed producer, without an appointment, to make an

12
00:00:45.622 --> 00:00:50.322
informal life-insurance inquiry or solicit a life application for an insurer

13
00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:52.022
authorized for that business.

14
00:00:52.862 --> 00:00:57.382
This is a specific exception, not unrestricted authority to bind coverage.

15
00:00:58.502 --> 00:01:02.702
If an insurer initially accepts an application from an unappointed producer,

16
00:01:03.082 --> 00:01:07.262
it must, within thirty days, either reject the application under the

17
00:01:07.262 --> 00:01:10.982
applicable law or appoint the producer and enter the required information

18
00:01:10.982 --> 00:01:15.722
in its register. Acceptance for processing is not necessarily acceptance of

19
00:01:15.722 --> 00:01:18.322
the insurance risk or a promise that coverage has begun.

20
00:01:19.236 --> 00:01:24.056
An insurer maintains its producer register and adds the required appointment

21
00:01:24.056 --> 00:01:26.556
information within thirty days.

22
00:01:27.536 --> 00:01:32.136
It also provides written appointment documentation within thirty days.

23
00:01:32.716 --> 00:01:36.636
The appointed producer keeps the documentation and a list of appointing

24
00:01:36.636 --> 00:01:41.936
insurers. With written documentation, the producer may act

25
00:01:41.936 --> 00:01:47.236
within authority before the insurer finishes the register entry.

26
00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:52.256
Appointment records stay available while the appointment is active

27
00:01:52.256 --> 00:01:56.236
and for at least five years after termination.

28
00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:03.256
Electronic records must be retrievable within ten working days after

29
00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:09.036
the Commissioner's request. A screenshot that cannot later be found is

30
00:02:09.036 --> 00:02:10.956
not a reliable record system.

31
00:02:11.646 --> 00:02:15.946
An insurer updates its register within thirty days after the effective

32
00:02:15.946 --> 00:02:20.946
date of an appointment or other covered business-relationship termination.

33
00:02:21.846 --> 00:02:26.666
Certain terminations involving suspected grounds for discipline also require

34
00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:27.906
notice to the Commissioner.

35
00:02:28.586 --> 00:02:33.006
Within fifteen days after that required notice, the insurer sends a

36
00:02:33.006 --> 00:02:36.646
copy to the producer using the prescribed delivery method.

37
00:02:37.106 --> 00:02:40.886
The producer has thirty days after receiving the notice to submit

38
00:02:40.886 --> 00:02:43.866
comments, with a copy sent to the insurer.

39
00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:49.486
Ending one appointment does not by itself mean the state has

40
00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:51.850
revoked the person's license.

41
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.206
Those are separate decisions.

42
00:02:54.048 --> 00:02:58.008
The Maryland Insurance Commissioner enforces the Insurance Article and can

43
00:02:58.008 --> 00:03:01.268
conduct examinations and investigations within that authority.

44
00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:05.988
Grounds for producer discipline include misappropriating money, intentional

45
00:03:05.988 --> 00:03:10.908
material falsehoods in a license application, forging an insurance document,

46
00:03:11.428 --> 00:03:14.568
dishonest practices, and other specified violations.

47
00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:19.088
The statute provides notice and an opportunity for hearing for the

48
00:03:19.088 --> 00:03:23.568
stated licensing sanctions. Denial, suspension, revocation

49
00:03:24.368 --> 00:03:27.148
and refusal to renew have different effects.

50
00:03:27.768 --> 00:03:31.368
An insurer's appointment decision is not a substitute for the Commissioner's

51
00:03:31.368 --> 00:03:34.888
process, and a producer should not ignore a lawful order or

52
00:03:34.888 --> 00:03:39.510
request for records. Under the producer discipline statute, the Commissioner

53
00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:43.560
may impose a penalty from one hundred to five thousand dollars

54
00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.710
per violation instead of, or in addition to, suspension or

55
00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:53.510
revocation. Restitution can also be required for financial injury.

56
00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.290
Other laws can create separate consequences.

57
00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:01.010
If an independent producer has good-faith cause to believe insurance fraud

58
00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.850
occurred, Maryland requires a written report to the Fraud Division.

59
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.850
Do not conceal a suspected problem to protect a sale.

60
00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:15.310
Preserve the facts, use the required reporting
process and cooperate within the law.
